; Ten cards a segment in (pc, kind, n, pvls, pnpk, and the ASP VOICED NOISE ALT VBAR cards of row pc of the
; phoneme table), two out: cf, the filter of a stop's closure (its voice bar,
; VBAR, when the stop is voiced and the sound before it is a vowel, sonorant or nasal; else 0, silence), and af,
; the aspirated filter (ASP) a vowel or sonorant speaks its first frame through when it comes right after P T K
; (pvls), a vowel only when it has more than one frame (a sonorant of one frame is then voiceless all through, as
; the R of "tree" is); else 0.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   pc       03-40: a segment: does it need the table
  04                    INP   kind
  05                    INP   n
  06                    INP   pvls
  07                    INP   pnpk
  08                    INP   asp
  09                    INP   voiced
  10                    INP   x
  11                    INP   x
  12                    INP   vbar
  13                    CLA   z
  14                    STO   cf
  15                    STO   af
  16                    CLA   kind
  17                    SUB   n3
  18                    TAC   va
  19                    SUB   00
  20                    TAC   out
  21                    SUB   00
  22                    TAC   st
  23                    JMP   out
  24            va      CLA   pvls
  25                    SUB   00
  26                    TAC   out
  27                    CLA   kind
  28                    SUB   n2
  29                    TAC   vn
  30                    JMP   ask
  31            vn      CLA   n
  32                    SUB   n2
  33                    TAC   out
  34                    JMP   ask
  35            st      CLA   pnpk
  36                    SUB   00
  37                    TAC   out
  38                    SUB   n3
  39                    TAC   ask
  40                    JMP   out
  41            ask     CLA   kind    41-68: the table's cards, then cf or af
  42                    SUB   n3
  43                    TAC   seta
  44                    CLA   voiced
  45                    SUB   00
  46                    TAC   out
  47                    CLA   vbar
  48                    STO   cf
  49                    JMP   out
  50            seta    CLA   asp
  51                    STO   af
  52            out     OUT   cf
  53                    OUT   af
  54                    JMP   rec
  55            pc      DATA  0
  56            kind    DATA  0
  57            n       DATA  0
  58            pvls    DATA  0
  59            pnpk    DATA  0
  60            cf      DATA  0
  61            af      DATA  0
  62            asp     DATA  0
  63            voiced  DATA  0
  64            vbar    DATA  0
  65            x       DATA  0
  66            z       DATA  0
  67            n2      DATA  2
  68            n3      DATA  3
